# ─── Android signing keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# release.keystore must NEVER be committed (Play Store signing, secrets-based,
# passwords via env vars — never hardcoded in source).
#
# debug.keystore IS deliberately committed (restored 2026-09-08 from commit
# 4d30188d): the actual distribution channel is sideloaded debug-signed APKs
# with an in-app updater, and that channel REQUIRES a stable signature —
# since it was removed on 2026-08-23, CI regenerated a random key every run,
# so Android rejected every update over installed builds (signature
# conflict). Play Store submission (if ever pursued) should use the release
# path instead.
android/app/release.keystore
*.keystore
*.jks
!android/app/debug.keystore
dist-admin/
dist/
